## Vercel Web Analytics Integration

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Next.js project.

### Changes Made

**1. Package Installation**
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 using npm
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the resolved dependency tree

**2. Layout Configuration**
- Modified `src/app/layout.tsx` to integrate Vercel Analytics
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the body section, after all other content components

### Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Analytics documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), I implemented the Next.js App Router integration pattern:

1. The Analytics component was added to the root layout file (`src/app/layout.tsx`)
2. The component is placed at the end of the `<body>` tag, ensuring it doesn't interfere with the existing page structure
3. The implementation follows Next.js App Router best practices by importing from `@vercel/analytics/next`

### Files Modified
- `frontend/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `frontend/package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
- `frontend/src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component

### Build Verification
- ✓ Build completed successfully with no errors
- ✓ TypeScript compilation passed
- ✓ All pages generated correctly (8/8 static pages)
- ✓ No breaking changes introduced

### Next Steps
To complete the setup and view analytics data:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics section
2. Deploy the application using `vercel deploy`
3. Verify tracking is active by checking the Network tab for analytics requests
4. View collected data in the Vercel dashboard after users visit the site

### Notes
- The Analytics component is lightweight and loads asynchronously
- No impact on page load performance
- Data collection respects user privacy settings
- The implementation is framework-optimized for Next.js App Router
